WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.880
So, here’s a statement that won’t blow
anyone’s mind: The SCP Foundation is really,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.050
really, really weird.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.090
And we’re not even talking about the actual
anomalies they contain.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.420
Sure, this top-secret organization puts in
the time and the effort to make sure menaces

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.930
to society like the Hard to Destroy Reptile,
the Scarlet King, and even the horrifying

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.681
Bad Joke Tomatoes stay behind lock and key,
but sometimes, you need to hold a mirror up

00:00:24.681 --> 00:00:27.870
to yourself and see just what the heck is
going on.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.080
I mean seriously, think about it.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:35.590
This is an organization that uses live human
beings farmed from death row as test subjects.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:39.050
Considering how rarely the death penalty is
actually employed in the Western world these

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.609
days, you know some shady strings are being
pulled there.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.420
And what about the O5 Council?

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.390
The leaders of humanity’s last line of defense
against anomalous chaos, and according to

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:53.559
some accounts, they’re a group of vain,
petty, and morally bankrupt individuals who

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:58.709
regularly use anomalies like SCP-006, the
Fountain of Youth, for their own personal

00:00:58.709 --> 00:00:59.769
benefit.

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:04.730
And don’t even get me started on the actual
scientists working under the Foundation’s

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.899
payroll, that’s when things start getting
even stranger.

00:01:07.899 --> 00:01:12.470
Of course, there’s Dr. Jack Bright, a man
forever changed by a chance interaction with

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:18.280
SCP-963, an anomalous medallion, and one of
Able’s deadly blades.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.630
Now he’s an immortal weirdo who’s equal
parts brilliant and a total nuisance - so

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.390
much so that there’s an entire dedicated
list forbidding all of his zanier antics.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.939
Then there’s Dr. Alto Clef.

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:33.079
Don’t even try to shake his hand, given
how much this ex-GOC wild card loves using

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:36.770
violence to solve his problems, you may draw
back a stump.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:41.560
He specializes in reality warping anomalies,
often wields a ukulele cause he’s just so

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:45.630
darn quirky, oh, and he’s very likely the
baby-daddy to a teenage nature sprite after

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.950
a dalliance with a goddess.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.759
Oh, and what about Dr. Charles Ogden Gears?

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:55.929
Sure, he may not look that strange to the
naked eye - he’s a man so dull and humorless

00:01:55.929 --> 00:02:00.560
that gray is his favorite color and he thinks
sugar on cornflakes is an act of unacceptable

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.960
decadence - but he’s got a whole lot of
strangeness under the hood.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.729
Like the fact he’s such an emotionally unavailable
father that his daughters across dimensions

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:12.530
have formed a splinter cell of the Serpent’s
Hand, where they work under the collective

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:15.610
pseudonym The Black Queen, just to spite him.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:21.130
Dr. Dan, through acts of sabotage, was personally
responsible for the worst SCP-096 outbreak

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:26.610
in Foundation history, leading to the end
of thousands of lives - just so he could receive

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.040
clearance to terminate the creature.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.100
And he got that clearance, on the condition
that the SCP Foundation would be terminating

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.500
him for his crimes as soon as the goal is
achieved.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.830
And then there’s...

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.460
Oh my gosh...

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.810
Did someone dress a dog up in scientist clothes?

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.220
This is the cutest thing I’ve ever seen!

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.480
Oh, this has just brightened my day.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.060
Maybe I was being too harsh on the Foundation
before.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.270
Whose dog is this?

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.470
“Excuse me, sir!

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.880
That is extremely inappropriate!”

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.290
Wait, you can talk!?

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.520
“Of course I can talk, you dolt!

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.820
I’m Professor Kain Pathos Crow, one of the
SCP Foundation’s finest minds in the fields

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.070
of advanced robotics and biochemistry!

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.390
I have a Level 4 Clearance, for 343’s sake!

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.030
I’m not some common bloody mutt!”

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.030
Oh...

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.440
My apologies, Professor Crow.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.970
I wasn’t aware you were a...

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.580
Well, a talking dog.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.320
“Well, yes, I imagine there’s a lot you
don’t know about me, isn’t there?”

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.840
I’m a little embarrassed to admit it, but
that’s true, Professor Crow.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.730
Our data on you and your work with the SCP
Foundation is a little sparse.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.760
“Here, take these files.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.700
These should give you a good primer.”

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.120
I suppose we better take this from the top,
then...

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.720
Professor Kain Pathos Crow, among a lineup
of extremely eccentric researchers, somehow

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.060
manages to rise to the very top in terms of
sheer strangeness.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.750
To get the most obvious fact out of the way,
yes, while he was once a human, an anomalous

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.280
experiment did result in him being turned
into a Labrador Retriever.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.500
How did this happen, you may ask?

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.290
We have the same question.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.780
Sadly, Professor Crow is incredibly reluctant
to share any details about this strange and

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.270
embarrassing incident, so we’re just going
to have to accept it for what it is and move

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.270
on.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.270
Everyone ready?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.960
Okay, good.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.720
Despite his strange appearance, Professor
Crow is actually one of the more scientifically

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.600
qualified of the Foundation researchers - it’s
no surprise that, because of this, he has

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.790
a relatively close working relationship with
Dr. Gears.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:29.070
So much so that he still refers to Gears by
his early Foundation codename, COG, a reference

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:34.100
to both the legendarily stern doctor’s initials
and a pun on his iconic surname.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:39.371
During one incident, Dr. Gears did tell Professor
Crow to terminate an anomaly - that was, for

00:04:39.371 --> 00:04:44.210
all intents and purposes, a human child - if
it presented any difficulties.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:48.430
This sours the wholesomeness of that previous
fact, so we’ll swiftly move on.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:05:47.490
Once again, Dr. Gears is just terrible 

00:05:47.490 --> 00:06:17.889
with kids.

00:06:17.889 --> 00:06:21.860
The other thing that’s kept him from being
turned into an extremely overqualified chew

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:26.770
toy for SCP-682 is the contents of his brilliant
brain.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:31.230
On many of the occasions when the O5 Council
have considered terminating him, he’s demonstrated

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:36.810
the fact he possesses vital and often irreplaceable
knowledge, saving his furry skin.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:41.560
A perfect example of the kinds of strange
scrapes that Professor Crow gets himself into

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:46.580
is the incident in 2009 where, without even
realizing it, he somehow traveled through

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.461
time and scared the living daylights out of
everyone.

00:06:48.461 --> 00:06:54.750
The details are best expressed here, in Professor
Crow’s own dictated notes:

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.120
18/02/2009

00:06:56.120 --> 00:07:00.669
In all my years working here, there have been
few things which have irritated me.

00:07:00.669 --> 00:07:05.520
Cause me physical harm yes, cause me undue
stress yes, cause me innumerable amount of

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.590
mental distress yes, but few things have just…
irritated me.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:12.150
Time travel is one of them.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:16.860
I went to bed on the fifteenth of January
year two thousand and nine at one thirty a.m.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:21.260
I woke up on February eighteenth at nine twenty
six a.m. of the same year.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:26.290
I hadn't moved, I had only nine hours of sleep,
and to me nothing had happened.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:31.060
Then after a slightly confused day amidst
the many cries of "I thought you were dead!?"

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:35.699
(among other things I might add), I discover
that I had been missing for the past month

00:07:35.699 --> 00:07:37.360
and three days.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:41.460
In that time, Sophia had completely taken
over my duties (though she had halted all

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:46.449
of my personal experiments), and was trying
her utmost to relocate me, while keeping my

00:07:46.449 --> 00:07:48.389
disappearance form the higher ups.

00:07:48.389 --> 00:07:53.110
Apparently, [DATA REDACTED] leaving me to
sleep in a small self contained bubble of

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:58.320
[DATA EXPUNGED] and making at least [DATA
EXPUNGED] which was eventually ruptured by

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.830
[DATA EXPUNGED] and sending back to this phase
of space and time.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:07.060
Needless to say I was… slightly irritated
to say the least.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.060
24/02/2009

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:09.060
Bah.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:13.540
They've had me in quarantine for nearly the
past week, observing me and running tests

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:18.180
to see if they can find any sort of strange
abnormalities with my physiology, my behavior,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.180
my anything.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:23.389
If I have one more hand shoved up my neither
regions, or am forced to look at one more

00:08:23.389 --> 00:08:27.220
bloody ink blot, I'm going to flip out and
go rabid.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.960
They say they'll stop the quarantine soon,
and Sophia says the higher ups still haven't

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.960
caught onto anything.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.510
I suppose I'm lucky in that count.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.490
Normally the only time they quarantine something
is when it's too dead to be of any sort of

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.050
immediate security hazard.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:42.829
Still, I guess I can see where they're coming
from.

00:08:42.829 --> 00:08:47.059
If it were my decision, I'd probably force
a quarantine too, and probably for longer.

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:52.029
At least they had the decency to give me my
clothes, my PDA and someone to dictate to.

00:08:52.029 --> 00:08:53.029
12/03/2009

00:08:53.029 --> 00:08:54.149
I'm still here.

00:08:54.149 --> 00:08:56.560
I'm still here and I hate it.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.180
Day in, day out, it's the same thing.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.390
Get up, eat, exercise, then simple observation
until lunch, then more observation until dinner,

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:04.390
then lights out.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:08.470
I'm not allowed anything other than the things
I already have, and even then, I only got

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.829
those because Sophia felt bad for me.

00:09:10.829 --> 00:09:14.920
I'm only allowed to use them every day for
an hour at most, otherwise they're also in

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:15.920
observational storage.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:16.920
All this wasted time.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:20.850
All this wasted time that I could have been
doing something constructive, something useful,

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:27.060
something interesting, but no, I'm stuck here
because of a wry twist of fate, forcing me

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.720
into this monotonous hell.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.149
They keep telling me I'll be let out soon.

00:09:32.149 --> 00:09:33.149
Liars.

00:09:33.149 --> 00:09:34.149
05/05/2009

00:09:34.149 --> 00:09:35.709
They've seen fit to release me.

00:09:35.709 --> 00:09:37.709
I almost thought I was going to die in there.

00:09:37.709 --> 00:09:40.980
Still, it almost seems strange to be out and
about again.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.699
But I do appreciate being back in my own quarters,
my own clothes and my beloved walker back

00:09:45.699 --> 00:09:46.839
by my side.

00:09:46.839 --> 00:09:49.329
Sophia has taken good care of the facility
while I was gone.

00:09:49.329 --> 00:09:54.100
I think I might actually leave that to her,
while I keep to my experiments.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.100
She seems to enjoy it a great deal.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.700
Suits her analytical mind.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:03.730
All of my personal experiments are still waiting
for me, with the exception of the 040 test

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:04.730
logs.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:08.279
They simply haven't posted their findings
yet, stating that they needed my approval

00:10:08.279 --> 00:10:11.800
first, so I'll have to pore through those
at the first chance I get.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.970
I'm interested in the progress she may have
made.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:18.930
Still, there is a good deal of work to be
done and I am more than ready enough to take

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:19.930
it on.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.579
After all, I have to make up for lost time,
don't I?

00:10:22.579 --> 00:10:25.899
It’s clear that life isn’t easy for poor
Professor Crow.

00:10:25.899 --> 00:10:30.329
Much like Dr. Bright, after experiencing the
mysterious event that turned him into a dog,

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:33.899
Professor Crow is both a researcher and an
anomaly.

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:38.509
And unlike the superficially subtle presentation
of Dr. Bright’s anomalous nature, it’s

00:10:38.509 --> 00:10:42.410
hard to hide the strangeness of a talking
dog in human clothes.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:47.480
This bizarre interstitial zone he occupies
forces the Foundation to keep him on an extremely

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:49.740
short leash - No pun intended.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:53.240
Seriously, Professor, it wasn’t intended,
I swear!

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.999
Anyway, the point is, Professor Crow isn’t
allowed to clock off at the end of the workday

00:10:56.999 --> 00:10:58.839
like his fellow researchers do.

00:10:58.839 --> 00:11:02.589
He’s forced to remain on site, almost never
appearing in public.

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:06.759
If the Professor wasn’t the kind of person
who could easily get lost in his work, a situation

00:11:06.759 --> 00:11:09.329
like this would probably drive him insane.

00:11:09.329 --> 00:11:12.890
Speaking of which, you’re probably wondering
by this point: Other than being the cutest

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.790
researcher at the Foundation...

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:15.790
Sorry, Dr. Clef.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.629
You’re special in your own way, we promise.

00:11:18.629 --> 00:11:23.279
What kind of work is Professor Kain Pathos
Crow actually known for around here?

00:11:23.279 --> 00:11:27.300
Professor Crow’s most notable body of work
is largely based on an opinion that’s pretty

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:33.300
controversial to hold around the SCP Foundation:
He believes that they should be actively utilizing

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:37.949
anomalies that aren’t dangerous in order
to further their collective goals.

00:11:37.949 --> 00:11:43.380
An excellent example of this is the cordial
relationship he has with SCP-040, also known

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.879
as Evolution’s Child.

00:11:44.879 --> 00:11:50.310
She’s a powerful reality warper who is able
to synthesize new anomalous life from pre-existing

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.740
living creatures.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:56.959
Professor Crow, who refers to her as Emma
in his personal writings, was initially training

00:11:56.959 --> 00:12:02.050
her to do this with SCP-148, the infamous
Telekill Alloy.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:06.459
However, he also filed a formal request to
go further, saying, “I think it's about

00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:11.610
time we started trying to utilize 040's abilities,
or at the very least, allowing her to use

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.139
them enough to actually learn how to control
them.

00:12:14.139 --> 00:12:18.940
She will not be able to rely on the SCP-148
hairpieces forever.

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:24.160
We theorized that as she gets older, her powers
will increase exponentially, possibly to the

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.739
point where her unconscious telepathy cannot
be contained.”

00:12:27.739 --> 00:12:33.889
He also, somewhat infamously, went ham with
a series of experiments using SCP-158, a frightening

00:12:33.889 --> 00:12:39.559
anomalous device known as the Soul Extractor
- which, contrary to its name, Professor Crow

00:12:39.559 --> 00:12:44.489
also realized could place removed souls into
other objects or creatures.

00:12:44.489 --> 00:12:48.869
This led to the creation of a being that Crow
dubbed “Zero”, because it was Subject

00:12:48.869 --> 00:12:53.649
Zero in his experiments to create a “composite
soul” using SCP-158.

00:12:53.649 --> 00:12:57.699
He spoke of this subject, somewhat creepily,
in his notes:

00:12:57.699 --> 00:13:00.459
“Zero would make an excellent candidate
for my assistant.

00:13:00.459 --> 00:13:05.100
It respects and admires me for its creation,
much as a child would an endearing father

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.100
figure.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:10.279
I have assured it that it would be treated
well, and that I will give it a host to the

00:13:10.279 --> 00:13:12.319
best of my ability to create.

00:13:12.319 --> 00:13:16.160
All that it asks of me is that it is given
a name other than Zero.

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:17.379
A name.

00:13:17.379 --> 00:13:18.379
Not a number.

00:13:18.379 --> 00:13:22.660
I told it to give itself a name, to christen
itself whatever it so wishes.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.760
It told me it would have to think about it.”

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:28.800
Like a lot of strange and fascinating figures,
everything you learn about Professor Kain

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.980
Pathos Crow seems to raise new questions.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:36.779
Is Crow just a mad scientist without a cause,
eager to perform bizarre experiments for their

00:13:36.779 --> 00:13:37.860
own sake?

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:38.860
Well...

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:39.860
Not quite.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:44.139
The sum total of all of Professor Crow’s
work is Project Olympia, a topic that probably

00:13:44.139 --> 00:13:48.020
deserves a whole video in its own right - and
do sound off in the comments if you’d like

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:52.129
to hear more about the deranged Frankenstein
project that Professor Crow has devoted his

00:13:52.129 --> 00:13:53.129
life to.

00:13:53.129 --> 00:13:57.751
You see, Project Olympia is Crow’s baby,
and also his attempt to play God: Through

00:13:57.751 --> 00:14:01.529
combining a variety of different anomalies
- including all the ones we’ve mentioned

00:14:01.529 --> 00:14:06.459
here, and several others - he would hope to
create an entirely artificial living thing

00:14:06.459 --> 00:14:09.920
that would serve the interests of the SCP
Foundation.

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:14.810
How exactly this would be beneficial to the
SCP Foundation is, admittedly, a little confusing,

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:19.489
but seeing this goal through to its conclusion
has become an all-consuming obsession for

00:14:19.489 --> 00:14:20.600
Professor Crow.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:24.529
He’s performed countless experiments with
a huge catalog of anomalies under the Project

00:14:24.529 --> 00:14:25.589
Olympia umbrella.

00:14:25.589 --> 00:14:30.880
He’s written reams upon reams of notes and
logs on the subject, and produced a huge number

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:31.880
of prototypes.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:38.100
He also used Project Olympia as a pretense
to remove even more souls using SCP-158, because

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.819
that just appears to be a strange obsession
of his, doesn’t it?

00:14:41.819 --> 00:14:45.959
Incidentally, we aren’t the only ones confused
about the exact purpose and value of Project

00:14:45.959 --> 00:14:46.959
Olympia.

00:14:46.959 --> 00:14:50.660
When members of the O5 Council finally got
a proper look at Professor Crow’s work with

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.600
the Project, they released the following statement.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:57.180
“All activity related to Project Olympia
has been discontinued.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:00.970
Overwatch Command has deemed it to be a gross
waste of resources, and permanently removed

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:05.809
support for the project, with personnel assigned
to work with it being moved to alternate sites.

00:15:05.809 --> 00:15:10.819
A hearing is to be held with the project administrators
to determine how the project was able to continue

00:15:10.819 --> 00:15:14.540
as long as it did despite the lack of any
concrete results.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.610
Prototypes and other equipment have been slated
to be decommissioned.”

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:22.459
Professor Crow took this news about as well
as you could expect, but in the end, he always

00:15:22.459 --> 00:15:26.639
finds a way to wriggle out and continue doing
whatever he wants to do.

00:15:26.639 --> 00:15:29.399
Because that’s what Professor Kain Pathos
Crow is all about.

00:15:29.399 --> 00:15:33.759
He’s living proof that sometimes, you just
can’t keep a good dog down.

00:15:33.759 --> 00:15:39.540
Now go check out “SCP Immortal Dr. Bright
Explained” and “Dr. Clef - SCP Foundation

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:43.679
Researcher” for more explainers of the SCP
Foundation’s most eccentric researchers!

